ble switch; advise updating the desktop app and checking Settings/Profile -> Pets and workspace availability. [Task 2]\n\n# Task Group: rtb-production-agent-demo static report UI\n\nscope: Redesigning and verifying the advertising-budget safety report generated by the RTB demo; use for authoritative renderer, no-script navigation, provenance labels, and browser-layout work.\napplies_to: cwd=/Users/enzo/rtb-12-page; reuse_rule=Reuse renderer paths and the script-free report contract only in this checkout or a verified equivalent; rollout provenance was captured from a separate Codex workspace.\n\n## Task 1: Integrate approved dark mint-green static report redesign\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-09-24T12-28-35-q3MS-integrate_report_ui_redesign.md (cwd=/Users/enzo/Documents/Codex/2026-09-24/plugin-browser-openai-bundled-x20-2, rollout_path=/Users/enzo/.codex/sessions/2026/09/24/rollout-2026-09-24T20-28-35-01a0d363-9b2c-78d3-ab6a-776a084bfea2.jsonl, updated_at=2026-10-02T10:26:01+00:00, thread_id=01a0d363-9b2c-78d3-ab6a-776a084bfea2, success; implementation workspace=/Users/enzo/rtb-12-page)\n\n### keywords\n\n- rtb-production-agent-demo, report-ui, src/rtb/demo/page.py, src/rtb/demo/static/demo.css, src/rtb/demo/flow.py, native-html-css, no-javascript, DemoState.is_sample, #flow-F1, #flow-F7, sample-provenance, pytest, ruff, mypy, css-target, responsive-layout\n\n## User preferences\n\n- When improving a report UI, the user asked: \"優化這個排版，有點不美觀\" and specified `rtb-production-agent-demo` as the flow reference -> trace and change the authoritative project generator, rather than leaving a polished temporary/generated HTML preview. [Task 1]\n- The accepted direction was dark mint-green hierarchy, one-at-a-time scenario viewing, collapsible decision details, role distinction through color/legend rather than repeated node-owner labels, and removal of supplemental information -> prioritize the main report path and reduce repeated secondary content. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- In `/Users/enzo/rtb-12-page`, the authoritative renderer is `src/rtb/demo/page.py`, styles are in `src/rtb/demo/static/demo.css`, sample data generation is `tests/demo/sample_data.py`, tests are `tests/demo/test_page.py`, and formal flow semantics are in `src/rtb/demo/flow.py`; rendered solid paths are validated against the formal graph. [Task 1]\n- Regenerate sample previews with `PYTHONPATH=src:. python3 -m tests.demo.sample_data`. `DemoState.is_sample` is the provenance signal for generated sample data; do not infer sample status from recorded AI mode. F7 follows “exceed total limit -> wait for approval -> human approval -> requeue,” not a direct block. [Task 1]\n- The project has an intentional no-script HTML security boundary. Use native anchors/CSS `:target` for scenario selection, `<details>` for disclosure, and CSS selectors/checkboxes for diagram modes; do not add JavaScript. [Task 1]\n- The validated completion suite was `PYTHONPATH=src:. /Users/enzo/rtb-production-agent-demo/.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/demo -q` (100 passed), `/Users/enzo/rtb-production-agent-demo/.venv/bin/ruff check src/rtb/demo tests/demo`, and `/Users/enzo/rtb-production-agent-demo/.venv/bin/mypy src/rtb/demo`. Browser checks covered one visible report for every F1-F7 selection, F7 disclosure expansion, no page-level horizontal overflow at 390px, `scripts: 0`, `ownerLabels: 0`, and no supplemental footer. [Task 1]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- Symptom: a temporary CSS/JS polish produced missing expected content, excessive SVG width, and an invisible Playwright target. Cause: the `/tmp` preview was exploratory and diverged from the report contract. Fix: implement in the Python generator and stylesheet, adapt tests to intentional contract changes, regenerate the preview, then run browser checks. [Task 1]\n- Symptom: a flow handoff label overlaps a node. Fix: adjust node widths, spacing, and handoff placement, then keep geometry