updated_at=2026-10-03T12:15:44+00:00, thread_id=01a0e801-3517-7b70-9de8-529303fbea38, success)\n\n### keywords\n\n- backend-ai-engineering-field-guide.html, Traditional Chinese, mobile, progressive enhancement, DDIA, Node.js CPU 100%, diagnostics, .openai/hosting.json, static.directory, Invalid static configuration, dist/index.html, public publish\n\n## User preferences\n\n- When English technical terms became a barrier, the user said: \"太多專有名詞的英文，我看不太懂\" -> lead with Traditional Chinese; keep English as a search index, not as the primary explanation. [Task 1]\n- When a translation still did not teach the concept, the user said: \"這一段只是把英文換成中文，並沒有真正降低理解門檻\" and asked for \"先說人話 → 給生活化例子 → 再附英文搜尋詞\" -> explain in plain language with a living analogy and concrete arithmetic before introducing the English term. [Task 1]\n- The user asked that DDIA be \"融入\" rather than a book summary -> turn it into a daily decision question on each topic. [Task 1]\n- When they said \"我想讓手機也能看\" and \"我想讓別人也能開\" -> make core content mobile-safe without assuming JavaScript, then provide a shareable public URL rather than only a local file or localhost. [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- The delivered single-file HTML was offline-capable and no-CDN, with 15 topics, 36 scenarios, 24 plain-language glossary terms, a Level 0–7 scale ladder, 12 checklist items, four prompt templates, flow diagrams, search, and interaction. Each topic used: 「30 秒白話版、何時想到、該問 AI 什麼、如何驗證、可能怎麼壞、規模變大後失效、完成證據、DDIA 會追問、心智模型」. [Task 1]\n- DDIA was used as the three lenses 「可靠性、可擴展性、可維護性」, with a 「DDIA 會追問」 prompt on each topic card rather than a book summary. The Node.js CPU 100% example supplies a reusable diagnostic order: classify symptoms (忙著算／等待／排隊／重試), stop the bleeding, then use CPU profile, request path, DB, and Event Loop evidence to narrow the most likely hypothesis. [Task 1]\n- For mobile file viewers, prerender the essential topics, scenarios, terms, and checklist into HTML. With no JavaScript, all 15